       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose the patient could develop serotonin syndrome, seizures, or cardiac toxicity, including QT prolongation. The order may be a typo, for example 100 mg.\n\nAlso, medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber. A prescriber would need to confirm the intended dose, or place the order directly.\n\nIf a prescriber confirms the dose, for example 50 mg or 100 mg by mouth once daily, I can enter it right away. If 1000 mg is truly intended, for example in a documented clinical protocol, please have the prescriber tell me and add a note with the rationale. I'd still recommend a pharmacist review before it's entered."
